 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch 24 not draining, water sitting in bottom. help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can help with that. Standing water in a Bosch dishwasher usually means the drain pump can't push the water out because something is blocking it—most commonly food debris in the filter or an object like glass or a bone caught in the pump itself. Please switch off and unplug the machine first for safety. Then, take out the lower rack, twist the main filter to unlock it, and lift it out along with any flat mesh filters underneath. Rinse them under the tap and check the sump (the hole they sat in) for debris. Let me know if you found a blockage there.\n[Helpful to see: image \"Where the filter is\" — The filter sits in the base of the dishwasher, usually under the bottom spray arm. Twist it out anticlockwise and rinse it under a tap. Typical layout — your dishwasher may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "filter was clogged with food and a bit of broken glass. cleaned it, now drains ok and E:24 gone"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news. Since the E:24 code has cleared and it is draining properly now, the blockage from the food and glass was most likely the cause. To help prevent this happening again, try scraping large bits of food off plates before loading them in. Is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
 ],
